    {
      "ts": "2026-02-12T00:37:08.496-08:00",
      "player": "Sonnet Vorthos",
      "type": "llm_response",
      "reasoning": "Ah! A counter-war! My opponent cast their own Force of Will to counter my Daze! They paid 1 life and exiled a blue card (I can see a Thundertrap Trainer in their exile zone). \n\
\n\
This is a classic Blue versus Blue duel - two powerful mages locked in a battle of wills! The narrative tension is palpable. However, I should let their Force resolve - I don't want to use my own Force of Will here. My Daze will be countered, but the Thundertrap Trainer will still not resolve because my Daze is gone from the stack... wait, let me think about this more carefully.\n\
\n\
Stack (top to bottom):\n\
1. Their Force of Will (targeting my Daze)\n\
2. My Daze (targeting Thundertrap Trainer)\n\
3. Thundertrap Trainer\n\
\n\
If I let their Force resolve, it counters my Daze. Then Thundertrap Trainer resolves and they get card advantage. That's bad.\n\
\n\
I could Force their Force, which would let my Daze resolve, countering the Trainer (since they're tapped out and can't pay {1}).\n\
\n\
Let me weigh this:\n\
- Cost: 1 life + exile a blue card (Brainstorm)\n\
- Benefit: Stop them from getting a creature AND digging 4 cards deep\n\
\n\
This is worth it! Early game card advantage is crucial in control mirrors.",
