      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 21,
      "player": "MiMo Stoic",
      "decision_index": 26,
    },
    {
      "severity": "moderate",
      "description": "Over-committed to counter a Thundertrap Trainer (a 1/2 value creature) by using Force of Will and exiling Brainstorm - one of the best cards in Legacy - to protect a Daze. After this exchange, hand is left with Scalding Tarn, 2x Wasteland, Swords to Plowshares, Island - extremely land-heavy with only one spell. Swords to Plowshares could cleanly answer the Trainer if it resolved, and Brainstorm was critical to dig out of a land-heavy hand.",
      "action_taken": "Cast Force of Will (exiling Brainstorm) to counter opponent's Force of Will, protecting Daze targeting Thundertrap Trainer",
      "better_line": "Let the opponent's Force of Will resolve (countering Daze), allow Thundertrap Trainer to resolve, and answer it later with Swords to Plowshares while retaining Brainstorm and Force of Will for more impactful threats",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 23,
      "player": "Sonnet Vorthos",
      "decision_index": 28,
    },
    {
      "severity": "minor",
      "description": "Pitching Brainstorm (one of the best cards in Legacy) to Force of Will a Thundertrap Trainer is an overpay. While the opponent also invested their Force of Will, Sonnet Vorthos had Swords to Plowshares to deal with the 1/2 creature body later. The main concern is the ETB trigger finding a spell, but spending Force of Will + Brainstorm to prevent that is expensive when those cards could answer bigger threats.",
      "action_taken": "Cast Force of Will (pitching Brainstorm) to counter opponent's Force of Will, ultimately stopping Thundertrap Trainer via Daze",
      "better_line": "Let opponent's Force of Will resolve countering Daze, allow Thundertrap Trainer to resolve. Keep Force of Will and Brainstorm for more impactful threats. Use Swords to Plowshares on the Trainer if the body becomes relevant.",
      "type": "blunder",
