      "player": "Sonnet Vorthos",
      "decision_index": 44,
    },
    {
      "severity": "questionable",
      "description": "Playing Wasteland without immediately using it to destroy one of the opponent's Islands is debatable. The opponent has only 2 Islands (both tapped) and a Snapcaster Mage. Destroying an Island now (or threatening to next turn) could be strong since the opponent is mana-light. However, the bigger question is whether to cast Swords to Plowshares on Snapcaster Mage first (while opponent's lands are tapped) before playing the land. With Tundra untapped and opponent tapped out, this was a window to remove Snapcaster Mage for free without worrying about countermagic. Playing the Wasteland first is fine sequencing-wise since it doesn't use mana, but not casting Swords on the Snapcaster while the opponent is tapped out could be a missed opportunity - though keeping Swords for bigger threats like a future Murktide from the opponent is also reasonable.",
      "action_taken": "Played Wasteland as land drop",
