      "decision_index": 45,
    },
    {
      "severity": "minor",
      "description": "Sonnet Vorthos passed the turn without taking any action despite having productive options available. The opponent has a Snapcaster Mage (2/1) on board and only two tapped Islands. Sonnet Vorthos could have cast Swords to Plowshares on the Snapcaster Mage (using Tundra for W) to remove the threat and deny future flashback value, or activated Wasteland to destroy one of the opponent's Islands (leaving them with just one land). Both of these lines generate meaningful advantage. Additionally, Phelia is listed in the graveyard so there's nothing to attack with, but passing without using Swords or Wasteland when the opponent is tapped out wastes a clean window to act.",
