    {
      "severity": "questionable",
      "description": "Sonnet Vorthos declined to cast Swords to Plowshares on Snapcaster Mage before it attacked, taking 2 damage. While they could cast it after attackers are declared (and still can during the declare blockers step or after damage), the decision to pass priority here without using Swords is not necessarily wrong since they can still respond. However, with Snapcaster Mage having already provided its ETB value (giving Stern Scolding flashback), removing it is reasonable. The real question is whether using Swords on a 2/1 is worth the card when Sonnet Vorthos is at 17 life. Taking 2 damage to save a Swords for a bigger threat is defensible, but Snapcaster is a key creature in the opponent's deck and they have no other board presence. Using Wasteland on Volcanic Island during their combat to deny them red mana could also be considered.",
      "action_taken": "Passed priority during combat, allowing Snapcaster Mage to attack unblocked for 2 damage.",
      "better_line": "This is debatable - saving Swords for a bigger threat like a potential Murktide from the opponent is reasonable. However, activating Wasteland on Volcanic Island to cut off red mana sources could have been considered at end of their turn instead.",
