      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 65,
      "player": "Sonnet Vorthos",
      "decision_index": 65,
    },
    {
      "severity": "minor",
      "description": "Sonnet Vorthos cast Murktide Regent before playing a land (Misty Rainforest or Wasteland were available). While Murktide can be cast via Delve using the 6 cards in graveyard (Flooded Strand, Force of Will, Daze, Scalding Tarn, Phelia, Ponder) plus 1 blue mana, playing Misty Rainforest first and cracking it would put another card in the graveyard, potentially allowing Murktide to enter with more +1/+1 counters (one more instant/sorcery exiled). Additionally, casting Murktide before land drop means if it gets countered, they've missed the opportunity to have an extra land in play. Also, casting the creature in precombat main phase rather than waiting gives the opponent more information. However, the bigger issue is sequencing: Wasteland could have been used to destroy the opponent's Volcanic Island before they untap, cutting them off red mana sources, but that should probably happen before committing Murktide into potential countermagic. Playing Misty Rainforest first, fetching an Island, would add a fetchland to graveyard for Delve fuel and provide an additional mana source as backup.",
      "action_taken": "Cast Murktide Regent before playing a land drop for the turn.",
      "better_line": "Play Misty Rainforest first, crack it to fetch an Island (adding another card to graveyard for Delve fuel and potentially getting a bigger Murktide), then cast Murktide Regent. Could also consider using Wasteland on Volcanic Island first to cut opponent off red mana before committing the win condition.",
