    {
      "severity": "minor",
      "description": "Sonnet Vorthos passed the turn without using Wasteland to destroy one of MiMo Stoic's nonbasic lands (Volcanic Island). With 4 lands on board including 2 Tundras and an Island, they have adequate mana. Destroying Volcanic Island would cut off MiMo Stoic's red mana source, potentially preventing cards like Flame of Anor. The player seemed confused about why Murktide Regent wasn't castable and passed without taking any action, missing the opportunity to use Wasteland proactively.",
      "action_taken": "Passed the turn without activating Wasteland or taking any action in postcombat main phase.",
      "better_line": "Activate Wasteland targeting Volcanic Island to deny MiMo Stoic's only red mana source, then play Flooded Strand as land for turn if possible, building toward casting Murktide Regent next turn.",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 96,
      "player": "Sonnet Vorthos",
      "decision_index": 104,
    },
    {
      "severity": "minor",
      "description": "Cast Flame of Anor before playing Prismatic Vista as a land drop. Should play and potentially crack Prismatic Vista first to have additional mana available after drawing two cards from Flame of Anor, and to get a basic land safe from the opponent's two Wastelands.",
