    },
    {
      "severity": "questionable",
      "description": "Sonnet Vorthos has two Wastelands and the opponent has Volcanic Island and Prismatic Vista as nonbasic lands. Using Wasteland to destroy Volcanic Island would cut off the opponent's only red source, potentially stranding cards like Flame of Anor. However, the opponent has 3 Islands plus Plains, so they still have plenty of mana. The decision to hold Wastelands is defensible since preserving mana sources matters when at 14 life and needing to cast Murktide Regent, but destroying the Volcanic Island to cut off red could have been valuable.",
      "action_taken": "Declined to activate either Wasteland",
      "better_line": "Activate Wasteland targeting Volcanic Island to cut off opponent's red mana source, potentially stranding red spells in their hand",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 102,
      "player": "Sonnet Vorthos",
      "decision_index": 115,
    },
    {
      "severity": "questionable",
      "description": "Sonnet Vorthos has two Wastelands and the opponent has Volcanic Island and Prismatic Vista as nonbasic lands. Activating Wasteland to destroy Volcanic Island during MiMo's postcombat main (after they've presumably tapped out or used their mana) would deny them their only red source and constrain their mana. With Murktide Regent in hand needing to be cast soon, keeping tempo pressure on the opponent's mana is important. However, Sonnet Vorthos also needs lands to cast Murktide Regent (which costs 7 minus delve), so sacrificing a Wasteland reduces their own mana. With 9 cards in graveyard, Murktide could potentially be cast for UU with enough delve fuel, so losing a land to Wasteland might be acceptable. The decision is debatable but passing up the opportunity to cut off the opponent's red mana (their only Volcanic Island) when you have two Wastelands available is worth questioning.",
      "action_taken": "Declined to activate either Wasteland, passing priority.",
      "better_line": "Activate Wasteland targeting Volcanic Island to cut off MiMo's red mana source, since you have a second Wasteland and enough lands/graveyard cards to still cast Murktide Regent next turn.",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 104,
      "player": "Sonnet Vorthos",
      "decision_index": 118,
    },
    {
      "severity": "major",
      "description": "Murktide Regent is on the stack and Sonnet Vorthos has Force of Will in hand (with no blue cards to exile for alternative cost, but could hard-cast it with 5 mana available: Island, Tundra, Tundra, Wasteland, Wasteland = only 4 colored mana sources plus Wastelands for colorless = UUWCC which isn't enough for 3UU). Actually, looking more carefully: Island (U), Tundra (U/W), Tundra (U/W), Wasteland (C), Wasteland (C) = at best UUUCC or UUWCC, which doesn't cast Force of Will (3UU needs 5 mana with 2 blue). They have UUWCC = 5 mana but only 2-3 blue. Force of Will costs 3UU = they need UU + 3 generic = UU + UWC or UU + WCC. With Island+Tundra for UU and Tundra+Wasteland+Wasteland for WCC = yes, they CAN hard-cast Force of Will for 3UU! Murktide Regent is a massive flying threat (likely 8/8+ with delve exiling instants/sorceries from graveyard). Instead of countering it with Force of Will, they played Flooded Strand, allowing Murktide to resolve. This is a game-losing mistake - Murktide Regent with multiple +1/+1 counters is extremely difficult to deal with, especially when the opponent has counter backup.",
      "action_taken": "Played Flooded Strand from hand instead of countering Murktide Regent on the stack.",
      "better_line": "Hard-cast Force of Will (3UU) using Island + 2x Tundra + 2x Wasteland to counter Murktide Regent, which is a must-answer threat.",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 107,
      "player": "Sonnet Vorthos",
      "decision_index": 121,
    },
    {
      "severity": "questionable",
      "description": "Sonnet Vorthos declined to use Wasteland to destroy one of MiMo Stoic's nonbasic lands (Volcanic Island or Prismatic Vista). MiMo Stoic has Volcanic Island as their only red source, and destroying it would cut them off red mana entirely, potentially preventing Flame of Anor or other red spells. However, Sonnet Vorthos may be holding Wastelands to use at a more impactful moment, and they need lands to cast Murktide Regent. The opponent has 5 lands including only one nonbasic worth targeting (Volcanic Island), so using Wasteland on Volcanic Island to deny red mana seems reasonable, especially since Sonnet Vorthos has 6 lands and Murktide can be cast cheaply with Delve (9 cards in graveyard means it could cost as little as UU).",
      "action_taken": "Declined to activate either Wasteland, passing through precombat main without action.",
      "better_line": "Activate Wasteland targeting Volcanic Island to cut MiMo Stoic off red mana. With 9 cards in graveyard, Murktide Regent can still be cast with the remaining lands (exile 5 cards from graveyard to pay for the generic costs, pay UU from remaining lands).",
      "type": "blunder",
